WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.040
- [Narrator] This is saffron,

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:06.000
and just one pound of
it can cost you $5,000.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.680
It's easily the world's
most expensive spice.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:10.430
The next most expensive spice?

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:13.410
Vanilla at about $600 a pound.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:16.313
So, what makes saffron
so wildly expensive?

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.463
For starters, saffron is a
complicated spice to harvest.

00:00:56.542 --> 00:00:59.470
Saffron comes from the
Saffron Crocus flower,

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:02.270
and each flower has three red stigmas.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:03.293
That's the saffron.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:18.940
Just one pound of saffron
requires 170,000 flowers.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:22.040
The purple flowers bloom
over a six week period

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:25.050
from late September to early December.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:28.163
There's also a specific
time of day to harvest them.

00:01:51.695 --> 00:01:54.110
90% of the world's saffron is grown

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:55.950
in arid fields in Iran.

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:58.503
But harvesting all that
saffron comes at a price.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:30.840
Most saffron harvesters are women

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:33.603
getting paid a maximum
of five dollars a day.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:39.380
Saffron is not only grown in Iran,

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:43.340
it's grown in Morocco, Spain,
Italy, the Netherlands,

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:47.300
Afghanistan, India, and
even in the United States.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.573
Why the US?

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:52.510
Though many Americans
have never eaten saffron,

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:57.510
the US imported 25 tons in
2013 and 46 tons in 2016.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.930
- What's so great about saffron?

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:17.290
Over centuries, it's proven
useful in many situations.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:19.763
Saffron is most commonly used in cooking.

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:34.940
- It gives paella its signature
flavor and golden color.

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:38.140
It's also used in broths,
breads, and marinades.

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:41.223
When saffron is broken down,
it creates a golden dye.

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:21.650
- People have tried passing
tumeric, red marigold petals,

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:23.790
and lily flower stigmas as saffron.

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:26.060
But the flavor and dye
is totally different.

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:28.540
In large quantities,
saffron can be a potent,

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:30.700
happiness-inducing narcotic.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:33.880
And research suggests it may
help reduce the symptoms for

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:36.920
Alzheimer's, depression, and PMS.

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:40.837
Who knew this little
spice packed such a punch?

